{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cstring>\n#include <cstdint>\nusing namespace std;\ntypedef long long ll;\nconst int MOD = 1e9 + 7;\n\ninline void read(ll &x) {\n    x = 0; char c = getchar();\n    while (c < '0' || c > '9') c = getchar();\n    while (c >= '0' && c <= '9') { x = x * 10 + (c & 15); c = getchar(); }\n}\n\nstruct matrix {\n    ll a[35][35];\n    matrix() { memset(a, 0, sizeof(a)); }\n};\n\nmatrix mul(const matrix &x, const matrix &y, int sz) {\n    matrix z;\n    for (int i = 0; i <= sz; ++i)\n        for (int j = 0; j <= sz; ++j) {\n            ll s = 0;\n            for (int k = 0; k <= sz; ++k)\n                s = (s + x.a[i][k] * y.a[k][j]) % MOD;\n            z.a[i][j] = s;\n        }\n    return z;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ll n, m;\n    read(n); read(m);\n    ll tmp = n;\n    int cnt = -1;\n    ll dig[75];\n    while (tmp) {\n        dig[++cnt] = tmp % m;\n        tmp /= m;\n    }\n    matrix f[75][35];\n    matrix g;\n    g.a[0][m] = 1;\n    for (int j = 0; j < m; ++j) {\n        for (int i = 0; i <= m; ++i) {\n            f[0][j].a[i][j] = 1;\n            f[0][j].a[i][i] = 1;\n        }\n    }\n    for (int i = 1; i <= cnt; ++i) {\n        matrix pre[35], suf[35];\n        pre[0] = f[i-1][0];\n        for (int j = 1; j < m; ++j)\n            pre[j] = mul(pre[j-1], f[i-1][j], m);\n        suf[m-1] = f[i-1][m-1];\n        for (int j = m-2; j >= 0; --j)\n            suf[j] = mul(f[i-1][j], suf[j+1], m);\n        f[i][0] = suf[0];\n        for (int j = 1; j < m; ++j)\n            f[i][j] = mul(suf[j], pre[j-1], m);\n    }\n    int cur = 0;\n    for (int i = cnt; i >= 0; --i) {\n        while (dig[i]--) {\n            g = mul(g, f[i][cur], m);\n            cur = (cur + 1) % m;\n        }\n    }\n    ll ans = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i <= m; ++i)\n        ans = (ans + g.a[0][i]) % MOD;\n    cout << ans << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final int MOD = 1_000_000_007;\n\n    static class Matrix {\n        long[][] a;\n        int size;\n\n        Matrix(int size) {\n            this.size = size;\n            a = new long[size][size];\n        }\n    }\n\n    static Matrix mul(Matrix x, Matrix y, int sz) {\n        Matrix z = new Matrix(sz + 1);\n        for (int i = 0; i <= sz; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j <= sz; j++) {\n                long s = 0;\n                for (int k = 0; k <= sz; k++) {\n                    s = (s + x.a[i][k] * y.a[k][j]) % MOD;\n                }\n                z.a[i][j] = s;\n            }\n        }\n        return z;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n        long n = Long.parseLong(st.nextToken());\n        long m = Long.parseLong(st.nextToken());\n\n        long tmp = n;\n        int cnt = -1;\n        long[] dig = new long[75];\n        while (tmp != 0) {\n            dig[++cnt] = tmp % m;\n            tmp /= m;\n        }\n\n        int sz = (int) m;\n        Matrix[][] f = new Matrix[75][sz];\n        for (int i = 0; i < 75; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < sz; j++) {\n                f[i][j] = new Matrix(sz + 1);\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Initialize f[0][j]\n        for (int j = 0; j < sz; j++) {\n            for (int i = 0; i <= sz; i++) {\n                f[0][j].a[i][j] = 1;\n                f[0][j].a[i][i] = 1;\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Build f[i][j] for i >= 1\n        for (int i = 1; i <= cnt; i++) {\n            Matrix[] pre = new Matrix[sz];\n            Matrix[] suf = new Matrix[sz];\n            pre[0] = f[i - 1][0];\n            for (int j = 1; j < sz; j++) {\n                pre[j] = mul(pre[j - 1], f[i - 1][j], sz);\n            }\n            suf[sz - 1] = f[i - 1][sz - 1];\n            for (int j = sz - 2; j >= 0; j--) {\n                suf[j] = mul(f[i - 1][j], suf[j + 1], sz);\n            }\n            f[i][0] = suf[0];\n            for (int j = 1; j < sz; j++) {\n                f[i][j] = mul(suf[j], pre[j - 1], sz);\n            }\n        }\n\n        Matrix g = new Matrix(sz + 1);\n        g.a[0][sz] = 1;  // note: sz = m, so index m is valid\n\n        int cur = 0;\n        for (int i = cnt; i >= 0; i--) {\n            while (dig[i]-- > 0) {\n                g = mul(g, f[i][cur], sz);\n                cur = (cur + 1) % sz;\n            }\n        }\n\n        long ans = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i <= sz; i++) {\n            ans = (ans + g.a[0][i]) % MOD;\n        }\n        System.out.println(ans);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.008670540526509285, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -3.790783375734463e-05, -2.47952248173533e-05, 0.0, -0.0005529781919904053, -0.20146244764328003, -1.1920922133867862e-06, 0.0, -1.68083679454